@nsobid-F19B2E01E1794F933A9720C1404BB6F6

# Bayonetta 2 1.2 - 60 FPS cutscenes

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Runs real-time cutscenes at 60 FPS instead of 30 FPS, at normal speed.
//
// Gameplay already runs at 60 FPS. Cutscenes raise a "30 FPS" request bit,
// and the main loop answers it in one place: it sets the NVN present interval
// to 2 and hands the frame timer a fixed step of 2.0 (the timer counts in
// 60 Hz frames). In gameplay the same loop leaves the interval at 1 and lets
// the timer measure the real frame time, clamped to 1.0 to 2.0.
//
// Removing the bit test sends cutscenes down the gameplay path, so the present
// interval and the frame step change together. That is why this does not run
// cutscenes at double speed: nothing is left forcing a 2.0 step per 60 Hz
// frame, and a scene that cannot hold 60 FPS still slows down the measured
// step instead of the playback speed.
//
// The request bit itself is left set, so everything else that reacts to it
// (voice suppression, camera and cutscene-only settings) behaves as stock.
// Pre-rendered movies are unaffected.

@enabled
0099146C 1F2003D5   // NOP (was TBNZ X8,#37 = the 30 FPS request test)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Bayonetta 2 1.2 (PlatinumGames "Hw"
// framework, PRJ_010, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
